# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded log2(1 + x) of BF16
#
# In B32: for x >= 0x1.6cp+12 log2(1 + x) rounds like log2(x), taken from the log2 tables. For |x| <= 0x1.84p-7 the
# Taylor terms x/ln(2) - x^2/(2 ln(2)) round correctly. A few exact or hard values are listed. Otherwise 1 + x is
# exact: its exponent gives an integer part, the upper 6 bits of its mantissa m pick r ~ 1/m and -log2(r) from a table,
# leaving log2(1 + z) for a small z = r m - 1. Round to nearest only: log2_1p(-1) = -inf, x < -1 gives the quiet NaN,
# log2_1p(+inf) = +inf, and a positive NaN comes back quiet. Uses CM_BF16_LOG2_T1 from Log2.te.
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binaryb16/log2p1/log2p1_bf16.c.
# Copyright (c) 2025 Paul Zimmermann
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard/Core

### B32 bit patterns of log2(x2) for 1 <= x2 < 2, where i2 is the lower 7 bits of the encoding of x2, with entry 0
### slightly above 0 so that exact powers of 2 also round correctly upward.
preset CM_BF16_LOG2P1_T2: @Array[U32, 128] <- [0x00800000, 0x3C37F286, 0x3CB73CB4, 0x3D08E68F, 0x3D35D69C, 0x3D626FD6,
